<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec_rc-circuits" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
	<title>RC Circuits</title>
	
	<assemblage component="implementation">
  <title>Implementation Notes</title>
  <p>
	The activities in this section are designed to be implemented in an interactive classroom, after students have completed the previous sections in the chapter.  Along with the activities in <xref ref="sec_lr-circuits"/>, they take about 50 minutes.
	</p>
  </assemblage>

<activity>
	<title>Making Sense of RC Circuits</title>
	<statement>
		<p></p>
	<p>
		As you saw in <xref ref="sec_rc-charge"/>, the charge and current for the <xref ref="RC1"/> are given by:
		<me>Q(t) = CV \left(1 - e^{-t/RC}\right)</me>
		<me>I(t) = \frac{dQ}{dt} = \frac{V}{R} e^{-t/RC}</me>
	</p>
	<p>
		Make sense of the capacitor charging equations in at least two different ways
	</p>
	</statement>
	<hint>
		<p>
			Good sensemaking techniques to try:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<p>
					What happens as <m>t \rightarrow \infty</m>?
				</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>
					Give a physical interpretation for the quantity <m>RC</m>.
				</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>
					What happens as the voltage of the battery increases?
				</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>
					Graph the charge and current as functions of time.
				</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</hint>
		
</activity>

<activity>
	<title>Parallel Capacitor Circuit</title>
	<introduction>
		<p></p>
	<p>Consider two identical linear resistors <m>R</m> connected to a battery <m>V</m>.  The switch is closed at <m>t = 0</m>.
</p>
<figure xml:id="fig_RC-parallel">
				<caption>An RC circuit with an extra resistor.</caption>
				<image source="RC-parallel.png" width = "50%" ><description>A circuit diagram with a battery on the left, an open switch on the top, and on the right is a resistor that is in series with a parallel network of a capacitor and another resistor.</description></image>
			</figure>
	</introduction>
		<task>
		<statement>
			<p>
				Sketch a voltage diagram just after the switch is closed.
			</p>
			</statement>
		</task>
				<task>
		<statement>
			<p>What is the current through each resistor at this instant?</p>
			</statement>
		</task>
				<task>
		<statement>
			<p>
			As <m>t \rightarrow \infty</m>, the capacitor will reach an equilibrium charge.  Sketch a voltage diagram at such an instant.  What is the current through each resistor now?</p>
			</statement>
		</task>
		
</activity>

<!--NO AI-->
</section>

